<br />
Before the 2014 numbering convention, each regional office ran its own four=
-digit sequence within the calendar year. A number like 2011-0447 is unique=
 only when it is paired with the office that issued it. Denver's 2011-0447 =
is the Braxton-Ferrer advertising examination you were sent; this office ha=
s its own 2011-0447, which is a different registrant entirely. Boston has a=
 2010-0447 and Fort Worth has a 2012-0447, and both of those turn up in key=
word searches for "0447" because the sequence portion is what people index =
on.<br />
<br />
When you request a legacy file, give records the region as well as the numb=
er, and if you do not know the region, give me the registrant name and I wi=
ll find the number rather than the other way round.<br />
